BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Mars Hill University
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251015T063000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20251015T073000
DTSTAMP:20260730T235909
CREATED:20240827T165937Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20240827T172604Z
UID:54383-1760509800-1760513400@www.mhu.edu
SUMMARY:Mars Hill CrossFit Club
DESCRIPTION:Open to students\, staff\, and faculty. We meet every Monday\, Wednesday\, and Friday at 6:30am at X-Caliber CrossFit in Weaverville. No need to be scared or intimidated\, EVERYTHING is modifiable and we have a lot of fun and share tons of laughter. CrossFit is more about community and building one another up through fitness and fellowship than anything else. If you have concerns or questions please reach out to Dr. Natalie Boone. If you are interested in trying it out\, just show up at 6:30 MWF ready to go.  Come on out and join the fun with us. (If you want to see some of the fun we have been having follow us on instagram at marshill_crossfit).
URL:https://www.mhu.edu/event/mars-hill-crossfit-club-2/
LOCATION:X-Caliber CrossFit Weaverville\, 7 Garrison Rd\, Weaverville\, NC\, 28787\, United States
CATEGORIES:CROSSFIT,Faculty and Staff,RECWELL,Student Activities
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.mhu.edu/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/crossfit-logo-featured-image.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Mars Hill University
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260731T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260731T190000
DTSTAMP:20260730T235909
CREATED:20260528T194112Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260702T163704Z
UID:66568-1785517200-1785524400@www.mhu.edu
SUMMARY:Mars Hill On the Road: Johnson City
DESCRIPTION:Mars Hill On the Road is a special series of gatherings designed to introduce Dr. Tracy Parkinson\, the 23rd president of Mars Hill University\, and to spend time with other Mars Hill alumni and friends to get updates about the Hill. \nAlumni\, parents\, and prospective students and families across the region are welcome. These events provide an opportunity to connect personally with Dr. Parkinson\, hear his vision for the future of Mars Hill\, and learn more about the student-centered experience and opportunities available at Mars Hill. \nAdmissions staff will be available to answer questions about Mars Hill! \nJoin us from 5–7 p.m. at Southern Craft Barbecue in Johnson City.
URL:https://www.mhu.edu/event/mars-hill-on-the-road-johnson-city/
LOCATION:Southern Craft Barbecue\, 601 Spring St\, Johnson City\, TN\, 37604\, United States
CATEGORIES:Admissions,Alumni,Featured,Public Events
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.mhu.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/marshillontheroad2.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Alumni Relations":MAILTO:alumni@mhu.edu
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Mars Hill University
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260801T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260801T163000
DTSTAMP:20260730T235909
CREATED:20260724T150416Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260724T154229Z
UID:66954-1785594600-1785601800@www.mhu.edu
SUMMARY:Alumni Event at SART performance of The Music Man\, Sr.
DESCRIPTION:You are cordialy invited to gather with fellow Mars Hill alumni at a matinee production of Meredith Wilson’s “The Music Man\, Sr.” The performance is Saturday\, August 1\, at 2:30 p.m. in Owen Theatre. The play will be followed by a reception and theunveiling of plaques honoring the legacies of Mars Hill professors of music\, Dr. Wayne Pressley and Mr. Ray Babelay. \nTickets are available at the Owen Theatre box office or at sartplays.com. \nThis production is made possible by the generosity of Mark Cabaniss ’82. \nGet Tickets
URL:https://www.mhu.edu/event/alumni-event-at-sart-performance-of-the-music-man-sr/
LOCATION:Owen Theatre\, 44 College St\, Mars Hill\, 28754\, United States
CATEGORIES:Alumni,Cultural Events,Featured,SART
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.mhu.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/musicmansr2.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Alumni Relations":MAILTO:alumni@mhu.edu
END:VEVENT
